## belay-trace

Write Goal and Evidence for irreversible or external actions, protected-branch
changes, deployments, security-sensitive work, human approval gates, and material
policy or architecture decisions. Add Review when a separate reviewer is involved.
For ordinary implementation, verification, and small reversible changes, do not
write a Work entry for every step or require a Plan, Intent Brief, or Delivery Map.

The repository-installed `.agents/skills/belay-trace/SKILL.md` provides optional
framing tools for heavy work and commands for trace updates. Preserve all
repository-specific human approval gates.

For heavy work, if the Skill is unavailable, run
`belay context compile "<task>" --format agent --budget 4000` before broad
history reads and preserve all repository-specific human approval gates.
<!-- belay-trace:end -->
